Link with \fI-lexpanse\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBexpanse_sync_set_t\fR and \fBexpanse_sync_map_t\fR provide thread-safe,
concurrent digital trie collections.
.PP
Writers employ optimistic lock coupling (OLC) over per-node version
words, allowing concurrent writers on disjoint key expanses to progress
in parallel.
Writers serialize behind an exclusive quiescence lock only for structural
conversions or upon retry exhaustion.
Readers execute an optimistic validation walk using seqlock version
words and Epoch-Based Reclamation (EBR).
The protocol is blocking optimistic lock coupling \(em a reader retries
a bounded number of times and then takes the writer mutex \(em not lock-free.
On the common path a reader acquires no mutex and does not block writers.
A reader that exhausts its retries falls back to the writer-excluding path:
it quiesces writers and takes the writer mutex, and writers wait until that
read finishes.
.SH READER HANDLES
For optimal throughput in multithreaded readers, threads should instantiate a
dedicated reader handle (\fBexpanse_sync_map_reader_new\fR) once per thread and
reuse it across queries.
.PP
A reader handle owns a single epoch slot and its pins are not reentrant:
calls on one handle from two threads at once are undefined.
A handle may be passed to, and freed from, a thread other than the one that
created it, once no call on it is in progress; every call releases its epoch
pin before returning, and
.B expanse_sync_map_reader_free
deregisters through the container's registry lock without reading
thread-local state.
Freeing a handle while another thread is inside a call on it, or after its
container has been freed, is undefined.
.PP
The one-shot functions (\fBexpanse_sync_map_get\fR) implicitly register and
deregister epoch participation on each invocation.
.SH ATOMIC READ-MODIFY-WRITE
.B expanse_sync_map_compare_exchange
stores
.I new_value
under
.I key
only if the key's current word is
.IR expected_value ,
as one linearizable step, and may be called from any thread on the shared
handle.
Absence is a flag, never a value, so every
.B uint64_t
is a legal value:
.I expected_present
false means only if the key is absent, and
.I new_present
false removes the key.
It returns true when the store happened.
On both outcomes the word the compare saw is reported through
.I observed_present_out
and
.I observed_out
(either may be NULL;
.I observed_out
is written only when that word was present), so a failed call hands the
caller the word to retry against.
A NULL
.I map
returns false and writes nothing.
.PP
.B expanse_sync_map_get_or_insert
stores
.I value
under
.I key
only if the key is absent, and returns true.
If the key was present it returns false, leaves it untouched and writes its
value through
.I existing_out
(may be NULL).
Of any number of callers racing on one absent key, exactly one gets true.
.PP
There is no callback form.
An update is a loop over
.BR expanse_sync_map_compare_exchange ,
which may run the computation several times, so it must be free of side
effects; the EXAMPLES section gives the loop.
.SH ORDERED READS
.BR expanse_sync_map_reader_first ,
.BR expanse_sync_map_reader_last ,
.BR expanse_sync_map_reader_next_at_or_after ,
.BR expanse_sync_map_reader_next_after ,
.B expanse_sync_map_reader_prev_at_or_before
and
.B expanse_sync_map_reader_prev_before
return the smallest entry, the largest, and the nearest entry at or after,
after, at or before, and before
.IR key .
Each returns true with the entry written through
.I key_out
and
.I value_out
(either may be NULL), and false when there is no such entry \(em which
includes a successor of
.B UINT64_MAX
and a predecessor of 0 \(em or when
.I reader
is NULL.
.PP
Each is one validated ordered search with the retry budget and fallback of
.BR expanse_sync_map_reader_get :
the entry returned was present, and every key the search passed over was
absent, at one instant.
Walking a range by calling
.B expanse_sync_map_reader_next_after
in a loop answers each step at its own instant, so the sequence is not a
snapshot of the map.
.SH MEMORY ACCOUNTING
.B expanse_sync_map_mem_used
returns the heap bytes used by the map's nodes and leaves, counted as
.BR expanse_map_mem_used (3)
counts them, and 0 when
.I map
is NULL.
It reads with writers excluded: it quiesces writers and takes the writer
mutex, so writers wait for it, and it does not belong in a hot loop.
Nodes retired to the epoch collector but not yet reclaimed are no longer
counted, although their allocations are still resident.
.PP
.B expanse_sync_map_mem_held
and
.B expanse_sync_set_mem_held
return the heap bytes the container holds from the global allocator: the
tree's own share plus what its epoch collector holds for it \(em freed
blocks past their grace period, kept for reuse, and retired blocks still in
their grace period \(em and 0 for a NULL handle.
They read with writers excluded, as
.B expanse_sync_map_mem_used
does.
.PP
.B expanse_sync_map_shrink_to_fit
and
.B expanse_sync_set_shrink_to_fit
return the collector's freed blocks to the global allocator and return the
bytes released (0 for a NULL handle), after which
.B mem_held
is lower by exactly that much.
They run beside readers and writers without excluding either: only blocks
past their grace period are released, and no reader can still hold one.
Blocks still in their grace period stay held until a later call, so
.B mem_held
may still exceed
.B expanse_sync_map_mem_used
afterwards.
.SH STRING MAP
.B expanse_sync_strmap_t
is the concurrent form of
.BR expanse_strmap (3):
an ordered map from NUL-terminated C strings to
.B uint64_t
values.
Its protocol, its container and reader thread rules, and its reader-handle
ownership are those of
.B expanse_sync_map_t
above: free every
.B expanse_sync_strmap_reader_t
before
.BR expanse_sync_strmap_free .
.PP
A key is read up to its terminating NUL, so a key cannot carry an embedded
NUL byte; such keys belong in
.BR expanse_ordered_bytesmap (3).
A NULL
.I key
behaves like a NULL handle: the call returns false (or 0) and writes
nothing.
.PP
The point calls follow the
.B expanse_sync_map_*
conventions.
.B expanse_sync_strmap_insert
returns true when the key is new, and otherwise writes the replaced value
through
.IR old_out .
.BR expanse_sync_strmap_get ,
.B expanse_sync_strmap_remove
and
.B expanse_sync_strmap_reader_get
write through their out-pointer only when they return true.
Every out-pointer may be NULL.
.BR expanse_sync_strmap_mem_used ,
.B expanse_sync_strmap_mem_held
and
.B expanse_sync_strmap_shrink_to_fit
behave as the
.B expanse_sync_map_*
calls of the same name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <inttypes.h>
#include <expanse.h>

int main(void) {
    expanse_sync_map_t *sync_map = expanse_sync_map_new();

    /* Writer inserts keys */
    expanse_sync_map_insert(sync_map, 42, 1000, NULL);

    /* Reader thread acquires a handle */
    expanse_sync_map_reader_t *reader =
        expanse_sync_map_reader_new(sync_map);

    uint64_t val;
    if (expanse_sync_map_reader_get(reader, 42, &val)) {
        printf("Concurrent read: 42 -> %" PRIu64 "\\n", val);
    }

    expanse_sync_map_reader_free(reader);

    /* update(42, v + 1) as a loop over compare_exchange */
    uint64_t cur = val;
    bool present = true;
    for (;;) {
        bool seen_present;
        uint64_t seen;
        if (expanse_sync_map_compare_exchange(sync_map, 42,
                present, cur, true, cur + 1, &seen_present, &seen))
            break;
        present = seen_present;
        cur = seen;
    }
    expanse_sync_map_get(sync_map, 42, &val);
    printf("After update: 42 -> %" PRIu64 "\\n", val);

    expanse_sync_map_free(sync_map);

    /* The shared string map, read through a reader handle */
    expanse_sync_strmap_t *names = expanse_sync_strmap_new();
    expanse_sync_strmap_insert(names, "alpha", 1, NULL);
    expanse_sync_strmap_insert(names, "beta", 2, NULL);

    expanse_sync_strmap_reader_t *sr =
        expanse_sync_strmap_reader_new(names);
    if (expanse_sync_strmap_reader_get(sr, "beta", &val)) {
        printf("String read: beta -> %" PRIu64 "\\n", val);
    }
    expanse_sync_strmap_reader_free(sr);

    expanse_sync_strmap_free(names);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SS Example Output
.nf
Concurrent read: 42 -> 1000
After update: 42 -> 1001
String read: beta -> 2
.fi
